            <ArticleTitle>Left ventricular size determined by electron beam computed tomography predicts significant coronary artery disease and events.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1236-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A novel method in the measurement of left ventricular (LV) area using noncontrast electron beam computed tomography (EBCT) was introduced and studied as a diagnostic and prognostic marker for coronary artery disease. Larger LV area measured by noncontrast EBCT was significantly associated with angiographic coronary disease and was a better predictor of coronary disease events than log calcium score.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
